### 1.1 Introduction to C
C is a procedural programming language.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
    printf("Hello World");
    return 0;
}
```

### 1.2 Operators
Operators perform operations on variables and values. Example: `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`.

### 2.1 If-Else Conditionals
Conditional statements let you make decisions in your code.

```c
if (x > 0) {
    printf("Positive");
}
```

### 3.1 For Loop
The `for` loop is used to execute a block of code repeatedly.

```c
for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    printf("%d", i);
}
```
